      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_a2c56854",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: mr-president-epstein-still-alive; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme uses a photo of former President Bill Clinton with the text 'mr. president, epstein is still alive' to imply that Clinton is somehow responsible for or complicit in the continued existence of Jeffrey Epstein, a convicted sex offender. This is a harmful meme because it attempts to link a former president to a criminal's alleged survival, potentially damaging Clinton's reputation and exploiting public outrage over Epstein's crimes. The meme is not directly abusive or hateful toward a protected group, but it is harmful as it spreads misinformation and conspiracy theories, which can incite public anger and undermine trust in political figures. The intent is to provoke shock and outrage by juxtaposing a respected political figure with a notorious criminal, thereby creating a false narrative of guilt or complicity.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_35a433e2"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
